.\" @(#)rstatd.8c 1.7 85/04/05 SMI; from UCB 4.2
.TH RSTATD 8C "4 April 1985"
.SH NAME
rstatd \- kernel statistics server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/etc/rpc.rstatd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX  "rstatd command"  ""  "\fLrstatd\fP \(em kernel statistics server"
.IX  statistics  rstatd  ""  "\fLrstatd\fP \(em kernel statistics server"
.IX  servers  rstatd  ""  "\fLrstatd\fP \(em kernel statistics server"
.LP
.I Rstatd
is a server which returns performance statistics obtained from the kernel.
These statistics are graphically displayed by
.IR perfmeter (1).
The 
.I rstatd
daemon is normally invoked by
.IR inetd (8C).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
perfmeter(1), services(5), inetd(8)
